## 03_3di dependencies

Requires Python 3.11 and a CUDA-capable GPU.

### Install

pip install "torch>=2.6" --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124
pip install transformers sentencepiece

### Model cache

The ProstT5 model (~11GB) is downloaded from HuggingFace on first run.
Set HF_HOME to avoid it landing in the conda directory:

    export HF_HOME="$PROJECT_ROOT/.hf_cache"
    export HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET=1   # disables unstable xet transfer protocol

The cache is reused across runs — no re-download needed after the first job.

### Notes

- torch cu124 requires CUDA driver >= 12.4 (In Phoenix HUJI SLURM cluster: use --gres=gg:g4:1)
- If the cluster only has cu121, upgrade to cu124 anyway — the driver is usually
  newer than the toolkit and will be compatible
- transformers must be >= 4.40 for AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM to load ProstT5 correctly